# Every pin for the stack. Nothing here is a floating tag.
#
# Base image is pinned by DIGEST, not tag. A tag can be re-pushed; a digest
# cannot. This matters more than it sounds: an image in this project once
# reported vllm 0.26.1rc1.dev0+g53f6dd5c6 while its own
# fused_moe/utils.py did not match that commit, which cost two debugging
# cycles. The image is authoritative; upstream SHAs are documentation.
BASE_IMAGE=rocm/vllm@sha256:b8a082f346d069376d35784250e38b23a043efe979408ae3a33d7c6b62ee3276
BASE_IMAGE_TAG_FYI=rocm10.0.0_ubuntu24.04_py3.14_pytorch_2.12.0_vllm_0.27.0

# vLLM source. The default is the fork, because it carries the four gfx90a
# patches that are the reason this project exists and that verify.sh gates on.
# To build against upstream instead, see BUILDING FROM UPSTREAM below: override
# on the command line, do not edit these four lines.
VLLM_FORK=https://github.com/davetha/vllm
VLLM_REF=v0.28.1rc0+mi210.7   # 14-patch gfx90a stack rebased onto upstream main 6fbb00b188 (2026-09-07)
VLLM_IS_FORK=1
VLLM_UPSTREAM_BASE=6fbb00b18874e27ba7d7adc0a3b8e93fee763ab1   # upstream main, nearest tag v0.28.1rc0
# The '+' is required, not cosmetic. vLLM builds its version with
# setuptools_scm, which parses the git tag; a tag like v0.26.1rc0-mi210.1 is
# not valid PEP 440 and fails metadata generation with
#   ValueError: Can't parse version from tag
# '+mi210.1' is a local version identifier: version 0.26.1rc0, locally modified.

# ------------------------------------------------ BUILDING FROM UPSTREAM -----
# A new model architecture often lands in vllm-project/vllm main long before any
# release tag carries it, and longer still before it is rebased into the fork.
# Ling-3.0-flash (BailingMoeV3) was the first case: absent from v0.26.1rc0,
# v0.27.0 and v0.27.1; present in main. So this is a supported mode, not a hack.
#
# Override on the command line -- the pins above stay put:
#
#   VLLM_FORK=https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm \
#   VLLM_REF=63550515b498261c820a1540be86a96e50802725 \
#   VLLM_IS_FORK=0 \
#     build/build.sh ghcr.io/davetha/vllm-mi210:ling
#
# Pin the SHA, never `main`. `main` is a moving target and the first line of
# this file is the whole reason that matters. build/Dockerfile probes whether
# VLLM_REF is a branch/tag and falls back to fetching it as a commit, so a bare
# SHA works here even though `git clone --branch` will not take one.
#
# WHAT YOU GIVE UP: all four gfx90a patches. verify.sh fails every marker and
# there are no AITER gfx90a code objects. Build the `gfx90a-unverified` bake
# target and tag the result -unverified so it can never be mistaken for a gated
# image. It still works: Ling served int4 at 4,711 t/s prefill this way, because
# vLLM's WNA16 oracle has no gfx gate and falls through to the Triton backend. A
# properly patched build should be FASTER than that, not slower.
#
# VLLM_IS_FORK=0 also downgrades the two fork-only acceptance files from a build
# error to a warning. Leave it at 1 for fork builds so their absence stays loud.

# Upstream AITER, unmodified. The fork davetha/aiter exists but carries no
# gfx90a patches -- the gfx90a work is not source changes to AITER, it is
# (a) binary repatching of the shipped gfx942 code objects and (b) patches that
# open AITER's dispatch. Both live in aiter-cdna2. Pointing at upstream is the
# honest description of what is built.
AITER_REPO=https://github.com/ROCm/aiter
AITER_REF=v0.1.21

# The gfx942 -> gfx90a ASM repatcher. Not a source patch: it transforms the
# code objects AITER ships, because AITER ships none for gfx90a.
AITER_CDNA2=https://github.com/davetha/aiter-cdna2
AITER_CDNA2_REF=v1.6   # tagged 2026-09-09. Two fixes, both required by this base:
                       # v1.5 -- supersede-detection also accepts upstream's own
                       #   _rocm_torch_fp8_scaled_mm_supported allow-list, not just the
                       #   fork's spelling of the same fix.
                       # v1.6 -- the CK int8 GEMM patch's gen_instances.py anchor is
                       #   re-derived: AITER v0.1.21 dropped a trailing '# noqa: E402'
                       #   the old anchor ran through. One anchor now covers v0.1.20
                       #   and v0.1.21.
#
# v1.5 is REQUIRED for a ROCm-10 base and is not cosmetic. Against vllm 0.28.1rc0
# on upstream main, the v1.4 marker no longer matches: the scaled_mm site is
# already fixed, but upstream fixed it its own way, so v1.4 reports
#   patched  pytorch.py  (want 1, found 0 unpatched / 0 patched)
#   1 site(s) did not match as expected.
# enable_vllm_aiter_gfx90a.py exits non-zero, add-aiter.sh aborts, and the image
# is committed with NO AITER. Measured cost of that on Qwen3.8-27B-W8A8, one
# MI210: vLLM selects TritonInt8ScaledMMLinearKernel instead of
# AiterInt8ScaledMMLinearKernel and decode runs at 16.5 tok/s against 48.0.
# v1.4 was the last ref that matched the 0.28.0rc2 fork spelling alone.
# v1.1 -> v1.3 carries the vLLM 0.27 spellings. 0.27 rewrote BOTH gate sites --
# supports_compute_capability became get_cdna_version() > 2, and register_ops_once
# dropped its decorator for an inlined guard -- so v1.1 aborts add-aiter.sh
# against this base. Each patch now keeps both spellings and detects which
# applies; zero matches still aborts rather than shipping a half-patched image.
#
# MEASURED 2026-08-14 on Qwen3.8-27B (48/64 GDN linear-attention layers), 2x
# MI210: enabling AITER changes decode by <0.5% and prefill within noise. Its
# flash-attention ASM only reaches the 16 full-attention layers, so there is
# little surface to act on. AITER is NOT a default win -- measure per model.
# Note VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=0 is baked into the image: without -e ...=1 at run
# time the patches are inert and a benchmark silently compares two Triton runs.
#
# v1.0 -> v1.1 is not cosmetic. v1.0 shipped the ATTENTION carve-out only, so
# every image built from it served int8 checkpoints through vLLM's generic
# Triton kernel -- correct output, no warning, ~1/3 the decode rate. Confirm
# with `probe/probe_image_patches.sh`: v1.0 images report ck_gate=no.

# Filled in by build/build.sh after a verified build. compose.yaml uses this.
# Registry digest, confirmed resolvable via `docker buildx imagetools inspect`
# rather than inferred from a successful push. Pinned by digest, not tag, for
# the same reason BASE_IMAGE is: a tag can be re-pushed, a digest cannot.
#
# Tagged by VERSION (mi210.6) rather than by date as earlier images were --
# a date says when it was built, not what is in it, and this one corresponds
# exactly to VLLM_REF=v0.28.0rc2+mi210.6.
DERIVED_IMAGE=ghcr.io/davetha/vllm-mi210@sha256:e2bbfc1ed711065b50703b8540d60a268dba69fdae8647b081de11ed9f1802f7

# AITER's JIT resolves against this exact Triton; a mismatch silently disables
# the ASM paths rather than erroring.
#
# 3.8.0 is what the ROCm 10 base ships, and on that base it is not a free choice.
# torch 2.12.0+rocm10.0.0 requires triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm10.0.0, and
# forcing the old 3.7.1 pin on top of it makes `import aiter` SEGFAULT (exit 139,
# measured 2026-09-09) -- which aborts add-aiter.sh and leaves an image with no
# AITER at all, the ~2.4x decode loss described above. 3.7.1 was correct for the
# ROCm 9 base and is kept here only as that note.
#
# add-aiter.sh installs this only when the running image does not already have
# it. That matters: the base's 3.8.0 is a ROCm build (+git4cff872c.rocm10.0.0)
# and a plain `pip install triton==3.8.0` would replace it with the upstream
# wheel of the same version number.
TRITON_PIN=3.8.0

# llm-compressor, for build/add-convert.sh only -- never in the serving image.
# 0.12.0.1 (the current release) pins transformers<=5.10.1, which conflicts with
# the 5.14.0 vLLM is built against; this alpha drops the upper bound. Installed
# with --no-deps and patched for Python 3.14 (build/patch_llmcompressor_py314.py).
LLMCOMPRESSOR_REF=0.12.1a20260701
